We'd asked them what their lunch was, and they, they of course ate it. Then we took the plate away. There were no more signs that they'd eaten. And ten minutes later we brought another lunch and said lunchtime and they all ate it three times each. The second lunch completely. Then we took that away, waited ten minutes and brought a third lunch. Each of these were full-sized lunches. And most of the time they ate the third lunch, twice I think one of them said, I'm getting a little stuffed, meaning their stomach was really getting full. But the point was that when you serve the meal, it looks palatable, you tend to eat it.
我们问过他们午餐吃什么，他们当然吃完了。然后我们把盘子收走。没有任何迹象表明他们已经吃过了。十分钟后，我们又端来一份午餐，说该吃午餐了，他们三个人每人把这份午餐吃了三次。第二顿午餐被完全吃光了。然后我们把盘子收走，等了十分钟，又端来第三顿午餐。这些都是全尺寸的午餐。大多数时候，他们把第三顿午餐也吃完了，我想有两次其中一个人说：“我有点饱了，”意思是他们的胃真的装满了。但关键是，当你端上一顿饭时，它看起来很可口，你就会倾向于吃它。

